# Text files are checked out with LF everywhere, Windows included (#217). Git for Windows turns LF
# into CRLF by default (core.autocrlf), and then a file differs from the one the tests, the hashes
# of the documentation site bundle and the template digests the editor compares were made from.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files are named, not left to auto's guess
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.gz binary
